research is licensed per directory, following the same split as the rest of
kindspec.

  *.md, design-findings/, findings/     CC-BY-4.0
  experiments/                          MIT, except:
    output that quotes SpreadsheetBench   CC-BY-SA-4.0
    output that quotes TmplEnron          CC-BY-4.0
    third-party sample files              their own licences

NOTICE lists every file in the three exceptions, with its source and
attribution. Full texts are in LICENSES/.

WHY THE SPLIT

The prose is a record and is meant to be quoted, so it carries attribution.
The experiment code is meant to be re-run, adapted and lifted into an
implementation without obligation, so it does not.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

No corpus an experiment reads is committed here; CORPORA.md names each one, and
its upstream licence governs it, not this file. The repository does carry a
few third-party sample files, and modified copies of them, under experiments/.
NOTICE lists each with its source, licence and copyright holder. Committed
measurement output also quotes excerpts of the corpora it measured, and that
material remains under its upstream terms: the MIT label does not cover it,
which is why the output files that quote SpreadsheetBench and TmplEnron carry
those corpora's licences in the table above.
